### Project ignores
tmp/

# The Fabro Enemy Unit Test comparison artifact. `just fabro-enemy-compare`
# writes this on EVERY run — it is compare.py's default `--artifact`, and the
# recipe passes no override — so the sanctioned operator entry point used to
# leave the working tree dirty every time it was used. It is a regenerable
# operator report, never durable state, and this repo's mutation protocol
# treats a dirty checkout as a workflow failure (several gates inspect the
# WORKING TREE, not the staged set). Kept beside the suite that produced it
# rather than relocated to tmp/, so the artifact stays discoverable.
/fabro-enemy-unit-tests/comparison.md

# Worktree-discipline pack — installed from the livespec-dev-tooling package
# (the single canonical source) via `just install-worktree-pack` / bootstrap,
# NOT tracked here. The from-package installer writes byte-identical copies
# into dev-tooling/ at bootstrap, mirroring how the commit-refuse hooks are
# installed into the untracked .git/hooks/ dir. The pack is six files: the
# four executable shell scripts (including the fleet's ONE workflow-edit guard,
# `check-no-workflow-edits.sh`, livespec-dev-tooling-fy02) plus the `worktree.just` and
# `branch-protection.just` recipe fragments the root justfile `import?`s. The
# per-ecosystem dev-tooling/worktree-hydrate.sh stub stays TRACKED (it is not
# part of the package pack).
/dev-tooling/worktree-lib.sh
/dev-tooling/branch-protection.sh
/dev-tooling/gate-run.sh
/dev-tooling/check-no-workflow-edits.sh
/dev-tooling/worktree.just
/dev-tooling/branch-protection.just

# The pinned fabro binary is fetched into the orchestrator-image build context
# at build time (orchestrator-image/build-and-verify.sh copies it from
# ~/.fabro/bin/fabro) — a 111MB blob, never committed. The version is pinned in
# orchestrator-image/Dockerfile's FABRO_VERSION.
orchestrator-image/fabro
# The plugin scripts tree is staged into the build context the same way (the
# build scripts copy .claude-plugin/scripts to orchestrator-image/plugin-scripts
# so the image can carry the mint-app-token CLI); never committed.
orchestrator-image/plugin-scripts/
orchestrator-image/plugin-meta/
# The tracked bd guard is also staged into the image context because the context
# root is orchestrator-image/, not the repo root; keep the staged copy out of git.
orchestrator-image/bd-guard/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/worktrees/
.codex
.idea/

# Playwright MCP browser-tool scratch (page snapshots, console logs) —
# per-session, never durable state.
.playwright-mcp/

